# QA Agent — Test-plan contract

- Validate with Ajv against `schemas/test-plan.schema.json` — not Zod.
- The same schema is the prompt contract and the runtime validator.
- Each case requires: `id`, `title`, `priority` (`P0` | `P1` | `P2`), `type` (`ui` | `api`).
- UI cases: declarative actions only — `goto`, `click`, `fill`, `expectText`, `expectUrl`. No arbitrary code from the LLM.
- API cases: `method`, `path`, and response asserts only.
- Enforce limits: max cases, timeouts, max Claude turns.
